          %h2#terminology Terminology
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            theory, what we call an ‘absolute value’ here is often called a ‘valuation’. However, there is also a more general notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valuation"} valuation
            used in field theory, which is what we call ‘valuation’. The notion of absolute value is also used in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+analysis"} functional analysis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+algebras"} Banach algebras
            are required to be).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
            (typically either a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            or at least an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domain"} integral domain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            over such), an
            %strong absolute value
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a (non-trivial) multiplicative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/seminorm"} seminorm
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valuation"} valuation
          %p
            This means it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\vert {-} \vert}\colon k \to \mathbb{R}
          %p
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in k
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert x \vert} \geq 0
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert x \vert} = 0
                precisely if
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = 0
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi x
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert x \cdot y \vert} = {\vert x \vert} {\vert y \vert}
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi x
                        %mo +
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ≤
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo +
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert x + y \vert} \leq {\vert x \vert} + {\vert y \vert}
                (the
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+inequality"} triangle inequality
          %p If the last triangle inequality is strengthened to
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi max
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ,
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert x + y \vert} \leq max({\vert x \vert}, {\vert y \vert})
          %p
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert {-} \vert}
            is called an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrametric"} ultrametric
            or
            %strong non-archimedean
            absolute value, since then for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in k
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert x \vert \lt \vert y \vert
            then for all natural numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi n
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert n x \vert \leq \vert x \vert \lt \vert y \vert
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert x \vert \lt \vert y \vert
            (and
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\neq 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi n
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert n x \vert \gt \vert y \vert
            = succeed "." do
              %strong archimedean
          %p
            Two absolute values
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert {-} \vert}_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert {-} \vert}_2
            are called
            %em equivalent
            if for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 1
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 2
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ({\vert x \vert}_1 \lt 1)
                  \\Leftrightarrow
                  ({\vert x \vert}_2 \lt 1)
                  \\,.
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
            of absolute values is also called a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/place"} place
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            equipped with an absolute value which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+metric+space"} complete metric space
            with respect to the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric"} metric
            is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+field"} complete field
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#trivial_absolute_value Trivial absolute value
          %p
            Every field admits the trivial absolute value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert {-} \vert}_0
            defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi x
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi otherwise
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\vert x \vert}_0 =
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  0 &amp; if\; x = 0
                  \\\
                  1 &amp; otherwise
                  }
                  \\right.
                  \\,.
          %p This is non-archimedean.
          %h3#OnTheRealAndComplexNumbers On the real and complex numbers
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            are a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequentially+Cauchy+complete"} sequentially Cauchy complete
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Archimedean+field"} Archimedean field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert {-} \vert_\infty}
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mn ∞
                  %mi x
                  %mi tanh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\vert x \vert_\infty} = \lim_{n \to \infty} x \tanh(n x)
          %p With the standard absolute value function defined, the maximum and principal square root functions could be defined on the real numbers as well.
          %p
            The standard absolute value on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi i
                    %mi y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %msqrt
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\vert x + i y \vert_\infty}
                  \=
                  \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}
                  \\,.
          %p
            These standard absolute values are archimedean, and with respect to these standard absolute values, both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+field"} complete
            and hence are complete
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/archimedean+valued+fields"} archimedean valued fields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            is in addition an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+field"} ordered field
            and as such also an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/archimedean+field"} archimedean field
          %p
            Similar norms exist on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+rings"} division rings
          %h3#on_the_rational_numbers On the rational numbers
          %p
            The standard absolute value
            %a{:href => "#OnTheRealAndComplexNumbers"} above
            restricts to the standard absolute value on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn ∞
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\vert {-} \vert_\infty}\colon \mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{R}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \lt 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert {-} \vert_{p,\epsilon}}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mfrac
                        %mi k
                        %mi l
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mi n
                      %mo |
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ϵ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left\vert \frac{k}{l} p^n\right\vert_{p,\epsilon}
                  \=
                  \\epsilon^n
          %p
            whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l
            are nonzero
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            not divisible by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            (and
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ϵ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert 0 \vert_{p,\epsilon}} = 0
          %p
            These are called the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-adic absolute values
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-adic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/place"} place
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
